# @meta.gap
> Compare your MetaCognitive Profile (MCP) from one or more extracts with a Target Cognitive Profile (TCP) and produce a structured GAP report

## PURPOSE
The meta.gap system analyzes the difference between your current metacognitive state (from extract files) and a target profile (role-based or custom), generating actionable meta-instructions to close the gap. This enables systematic cognitive improvement aligned with specific role requirements.

## WHEN TO USE
- After collecting 1+ meta extracts
- When preparing for a new role or project type
- For tracking cognitive evolution over time
- When feeling misaligned with project requirements
- Before creating new persistent rules from meta-instructions

## INPUT
- **role**: `<CTO | CPO | CMO | CEO | Frontend | Backend | UX | Web3 | custom | ask>`
- **target_profile_json**: (optional, required if role=custom) — JSON with 6 MCP axes
- **extract_files**: `<list of meta.extract.*.mdc | ask>` — one or more extract files
- **timestamp**: `<ISO UTC>` — default: auto-generated
- **author**: `<string>` — optional user identifier

